{"decision":{"text":"Adopt a rebuilt stage-2 recipe that teaches the image slots to keep the page's words, or keep today's stage-2 and finetune recipe. The main candidate is a larger share of page transcription on document pages. Three side options are tested too: transcription windows from anywhere on the page, fp32 master weights, and a finetune with the judged-wrong teacher labels dropped.","evidence":"rebuild stage 2 so the image slots keep the page's words.","file":""},"decisive":{"answer":"yes","why":"Each change is compared with a second seed of today's stage-2 recipe. That control runs on the same seed and the same code, and is finetuned the same way. The first test is page word recall: the share of a page's words the model can rebuild from its slots. It is read on untrained dense pages and on the eval documents' gold pages. It has a known-positive control (the overfit model, recall .921) and a self-pair check, and it is read through the same readout script slotcheck validated. The second test is judge accuracy on 1,500 paired document questions, with photos and text as guards, the uncompressed decoder as reference, and a finetune-level noise floor. I checked the code. The transcription-share launcher sets the per-source task mix only on rows whose source is 'pdfa' or 'wiki-ss'. On those rows the collator's 'text' task is the text-compression forgetting guard, so the text set is the right guard. The finetune launcher starts each arm from its own stage-2 model with R's exact recipe. The cleaned-label arm starts from the recorded stage 2. A config check kills any run whose resolved config differs from the recorded one beyond the allowed fields. The sets the law names exist: the two dense-page sets, the text set and the overfit model. Slotcheck showed that about 5 of the 19.4 lost judge points sit in the page's words, so the document set can show a gain. A pass, a fail or a promising result each lead to a different choice. One caution, not a gap: the law itself forecasts a document gain of 1 to 3 points against a 3-point bar. So the most likely outcome is 'promising', which leads to the planned one-time repeat at seed 43 (about 24 GPU-h, owner's approval needed).","evidence":"PASS = documents ≥ +3 pt with the CI above 0 AND above the finetune floor, and neither photos nor text loses ≥ 3 pt","file":""},"missing":[],"summary":"Yes: this campaign can settle whether to adopt a rebuilt stage-2 recipe that makes the image slots keep the page's words. Each change is compared with a second seed of today's recipe on the same code. It is measured first on page word recall (the share of a page's words rebuilt from its slots, with a known-positive control), then on judge accuracy for document questions, with photos and text as guards. Nothing is missing. Expect a likely 'promising' result: the law forecasts a 1 to 3 point document gain against a 3-point bar, which would trigger the planned seed-43 repeat (about 24 GPU-h, owner's approval needed)."}
